title: Entra ID Device Code Flow Sign-in From Unfamiliar Location or Application
id: 4b1c7f22-9d3e-4c5a-8e21-0d50a2026dc1
status: experimental
description: Successful device-code-flow token issuance (T1528) in risky context. Device code phishing bypasses MFA because the victim completes MFA on the attacker's behalf on a genuine Microsoft page.
author: Eswar Mahalingam (GraySentinel DSOU, candidate 13)
date: 2026-09-17
references:
  - https://learn.microsoft.com/entra/identity-platform/v2-oauth2-device-code
  - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1528/
tags:
  - attack.credential_access
  - attack.t1528
  - attack.t1078.004
logsource:
  product: azure
  service: signinlogs
detection:
  device_code:
    AuthenticationProtocol: 'deviceCode'
  success:
    ResultType: 0
  risky_context:
    - RiskLevelDuringSignIn: ['medium', 'high']
    - ConditionalAccessStatus: 'notApplied'
    - AppDisplayName: ['Microsoft Office', 'Microsoft Graph Command Line Tools', 'Microsoft Authentication Broker']
  condition: device_code and success and risky_context
falsepositives:
  - Azure CLI / PowerShell / Teams Rooms / Intune enrolment from known admin workstations (allow-list AppId)
level: high
